      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To solve the expression \\( 19^2 - 17^2 + 15^2 - 13^2 + 11^2 - 9^2 + 7^2 - 5^2 + 3^2 - 1^2 \\), we will use the difference of squares formula, which states that \\( a^2 - b^2 = (a+b)(a-b) \\). Let's group and simplify the terms step by step.\n\nFirst, group the positive and negative terms separately:\n\\[ (19^2 - 17^2) + (15^2 - 13^2) + (11^2 - 9^2) + (7^2 - 5^2) + (3^2 - 1^2) \\]\n\nUsing the difference of squares formula:\n\\[ a^2 - b^2 = (a + b)(a - b) \\]\nwe can rewrite each pair as follows:\n\\[ 19^2 - 17^2 = (19 + 17)(19 - 17) = 36 \\cdot 2 = 72 \\]\n\\[ 15^2 - 13^2 = (15 + 13)(15 - 13) = 28 \\cdot 2 = 56 \\]\n\\[ 11^2 - 9^2 = (11 + 9)(11 - 9) = 20 \\cdot 2 = 40 \\]\n\\[ 7^2 - 5^2 = (7 + 5)(7 - 5) = 12 \\cdot 2 = 24 \\]\n\\[ 3^2 - 1^2 = (3 + 1)(3 - 1) = 4 \\cdot 2 = 8 \\]\n\nNow substitute these results back into the original expression:\n\\[ 72 + 56 + 40 + 24 + 8 \\]\n\nNext, perform the addition step by step:\nFirst, add 72 and 56:\n\\[ 72 + 56 = 128 \\]\n\nNext, add 40 to the result:\n\\[ 128 + 40 = 168 \\]\n\nThen, add 24 to the result:\n\\[ 168 + 24 = 192 \\]\n\nFinally, add 8 to the result:\n\\[ 192 + 8 = 200 \\]\n\nThus, the value of the expression is:\n\\[ \\boxed{200} \\]",
